{
  "format": [
    "Shared test vectors for the history filter. Two suites read this file: webui/test/history.test.mjs (Node) and the router test in lorawan-sniffer/src/api/message_tests.rs (Rust). Both must give the same answers.",
    "Top-level keys: format (this text), labels, records, cases.",
    "labels: object, identifier -> label text. The identifier is a DevAddr or a DevEUI exactly as a record carries it (EUIs colon-separated, upper case). A record's label is the one stored for its identifier, which is dev_addr, else dev_eui. Store these through the label store (they are what GET /api/labels returns).",
    "records: array of the stored records, sorted by timestamp ascending (true time order), ids unique. Fields: id, timestamp (ISO 8601 UTC with Z; 0, 3 or 6 fraction digits, as the sniffer writes them), mtype (MType name), status (Forwarded | Blocked | Captured), gateway_eui (string or null), dev_addr (string or null), dev_eui (string or null), malformed (null, crc, mhdr or length). Every other field of a record is irrelevant to the filters: use any value. A record can have both dev_addr and dev_eui (r10): its identifier, for labels, is the DevAddr.",
    "cases: array of {name, filter, query, expect, expectMalformed}. Names are unique.",
    "filter: the browser's HistoryFilter with the time bound as text: {device, mtypes, status, from, gateway, hideMalformed}. device is the text as typed (never trimmed). mtypes: MType names, empty = any. status: all | Forwarded | Blocked | Captured. gateway: exact text, empty = any. from: ISO 8601 text with milliseconds and Z, the inclusive lower bound, or null. hideMalformed: true leaves malformed records out. The Node suite converts from to epoch milliseconds; the Rust suite does not read filter at all.",
    "query: the filter part of the /api/messages query string, exactly as the browser builds it: from, device, mtype, status, gateway, malformed, in that order, each value percent-encoded (a + is %2B, a space %20), filters that select everything left out, and malformed=exclude only when hideMalformed is true. It can be empty. Rust: GET /api/messages?<query>&newest=true&count=true&limit=5000 (when query is empty, drop the first &). status is sent as in the filter (Forwarded), which the server accepts in any case.",
    "expect: the ids of the records the request must return, in the order returned (oldest first, which is the order of records). Rust: the response ids equal expect, and X-Total-Count equals its length. The Node suite checks the same list with matchesFilter.",
    "expectMalformed: the number of malformed records that match every filter except hideMalformed, whether hideMalformed hides them or not. Rust: X-Malformed-Count equals it. The Node suite checks it with countsAsMalformed."
  ],
